DECISIONS 213, 442, CODEGEN.md §7.9: a define name that E8011 refuses (here Len, a name every container has, which canon_runtime.h also uses) is no project define for the foreign-define rule: its finding is the defining package's E8011, and no E8005 follows in the package whose container has a Len of its own.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// Words; the defines keep the names.
enum Word @cpp(defines: "") {
  /// A name the container members reserve.
  Len
}

emit cpp { out: "@features/a", namespace: "a", mode: types }
-- b/b.canon --
package b

/// A tier.
record Tier {
  /// Its rank.
  rank: Int
}

/// The tiers.
let tiers: table Tier = {
  one { rank: 1 }
}

emit cpp { out: "@features/b", namespace: "b", mode: baked }
emit json { out: "out/" }
-- b.tiers.json --
{ "one": { "rank": 1 } }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8011]  a/a.canon:6:3
  Len, the C++ name derived for a.Word.Len, is a keyword or a reserved name

1 error, 0 warnings in 2 packages (…)
